<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alamgir II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1699">1699</a>–<a href="/years/1759">1759</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alamgir II was Mughal emperor from 1754 to 1759, a son of Jahandar Shah placed on the throne by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi-ud-din-khan-imad-ul-mulk">Ghazi-ud-din Khan Imad-ul-Mulk</a>. He held little real power, as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a> sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1757 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> and the vizier competed for control. Fearing that the emperor was conspiring against him, Imad-ul-Mulk had him murdered in 1759.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alamgir-ii.jpg" alt="Alamgir II" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sukha Luhar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alamgir_II_of_India.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
